  "Description": {
    "Cost": 34807590,
    "UIName": "Leliourium",
    "Id": "chassisdef_leliourium_I-LEM-OA",
    "Name": "Leliourium",
    "Details": "The second configuration of the Leliourium, named 'Paimon', is an indirect fire role. The full focus on missiles is very evident with its four Artemis IV FCS supported Rotary LRM-20 launchers in the arms and the Arrow IV mounted in the Left Torso. An advanced ton targeting computer further enhances the 'Mechs capabilities, enabling both improved clustering and multi-target capabilities. The large weakness of the A configuration is the lack of any weapons capable of defensive duties.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Wrath of Blake</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.39</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Omni</color>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_leliourum"
  },
  "VariantName": "I-LEM-OA",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitUpperLeft",
      "ArmLimitUpperRight",
      "OmniMech",
      "Superheavy",
      "mr-resize-1.41"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Infernal Superheavy",
  "YangsThoughts": "When the news of Precentor Vapula's Celestial series of 'Mechs reached Precentor Destral VII, he refused to have his devotion be outdone. Throwing all available, and unavailable, resources at the task, Precentor Destral VII's design team created the Leliorium, a 200t Omnimech, named after the highest rank of demons in the Ars Goetia, as compared to the Celestial series' angels. Furthering the point that these are not just the Celestials on steroids, each configuration is further named after one of the nine demon kings.  Each one brings to bear the cutting edge of experimental weaponry and armor, such as the Exsecratio Stealth Armor and the Seraphim Electronic Warfare Suite. The final check, before each unit is released from the factory, is a holy blessing by 6 high Blakist Priests, ensuring that the pilot, and 'Mech, are well taken care of by Blake.",
